    "modified": true,
    "modifications": "2 real Interstate 5 and Lake Samish paths stitched through the OSM graph, heading Gaussian-smoothed, positions re-integrated from heading, then pinned back onto the real junctions (largest drift closed 43.2 m, spread back along each line), resampled at 2 m with curvature from the sampled positions; land elevation from 3DEP low-pass filtered, bridge decks synthesized (3DEP is bare earth); lanes simplified to the configured cross-section; junction connector roads synthesized (a turn, a straight and a turn)"
  },
  "meta": {
    "status": "live",
    "notes": "A real-road network (run W-S; interview, 2026-10-02: map-based networks, multi-lane highways, junction choices): Interstate 5 southbound over the Chuckanut Mountains, four lanes and a grass median, and Lake Samish's north and east shore roads, which leave it at exit 246 and rejoin it at the Nulle Road on-ramp (exit 242). Junction pieces and connector roads are synthesized; the lines are pinned to the real junctions (closure)."
  }
